---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { event } from '../data/catalogue';
import { analyticsMeasurementId } from '../lib/analytics-consent';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy and cookies"
  description="Choose whether CreaTech Showcase can use Google Analytics to understand visits."
>
  <div class="wrap section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your choice</p>
    <h1>Privacy and cookies</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Visitor statistics are optional</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics to understand visits to the public exhibition
        guide. Analytics cookies and visitor measurement stay off until you
        choose “Allow analytics”. Choosing “No thanks” does not change how the
        site works.
      </p>
      <button type="button" class="button" data-analytics-settings hidden>
        Change analytics choice
      </button>
      <noscript>
        <p>JavaScript is off, so analytics is off too.</p>
      </noscript>
      <h2>What Google receives</h2>
      <p>
        If you allow analytics, Google receives the public pages you visit and
        information such as your device, browser, language and approximate
        location. Cookies help count visits and returning visitors. We do not
        use this data for advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        We leave private workspaces, reminder forms and your shortlist out of
        analytics. We do not send form answers, email addresses, URL query
        strings or fragments, or the address of the page you came from.
        Automatic tracking of searches, downloads, links and form interactions
        is off.
      </p>
      <p>
        The public guide loads a Google script to verify this website in Google
        Search Console. Loading it connects your browser to Google, even if you
        decline analytics. Visitor measurement remains disabled until you allow
        it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">
          Google’s privacy policy
        </a>{' '}
        for details of how Google handles data.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies and saved choices</h2>
      <p>
        We remember your choice in this browser for 180 days. If you allow
        analytics, Google’s <code>_ga</code> and{' '}
        <code>{`_ga_${analyticsMeasurementId.slice(2)}`}</code> cookies last for
        up to 90 days. Declining later stops measurement and removes these
        cookies from this site. It does not erase statistics already sent.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your shortlist is saved separately in this browser. Changing your
        analytics choice does not change your shortlist.
      </p>
      <h2>Change your choice</h2>
      <p>
        Use “Analytics settings” in the footer at any time. Your choice applies
        to this browser; make it again if you use another browser or clear its
        saved data.
      </p>
      {event.publicContact && (
        <p>
          For questions, contact{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${event.publicContact.email}`}>
            {event.publicContact.email}
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      )}
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
